{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Gorgeous George is the third solo studio album by Scottish musician Edwyn Collins.","title":"Gorgeous George (album)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The album was recorded at New River in London, with Collins acting as the producer.","title":"Gorgeous George (album)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Gillan's Inn is an album by Ian Gillan in celebration of his 40 years as a singer.","title":"Gillan's Inn"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The first release was a DualDisc composed of both a CD and a DVD side.","title":"Gillan's Inn"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The CD featured re-recorded tracks from all eras of Ian Gillan's singing career.","title":"Gillan's Inn"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" In a recent interview Gillan observed that, despite the number of participants and guest appearances, this was the easiest project he ever put together.","title":"Gillan's Inn"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Toolbox is the second solo album by Ian Gillan originally released only in Europe, Japan and Brazil on German label EastWest.","title":"Toolbox (album)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was Gillan's last album before his second comeback with Deep Purple in August 1992.","title":"Toolbox (album)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The subsequent mammoth 10-month tour, which crossed Europe and South America, proved Ian Gillan to be a strong live attraction.","title":"Toolbox (album)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Although "Toolbox" wasn't a big commercial success it is considered by many as one of Gillan's finest records.","title":"Toolbox (album)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The album was finally released domestically in the USA in 1997.","title":"Toolbox (album)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Dreamcatcher is a studio album by Ian Gillan, released in September 1997 in Japan, October 1997 in the United Kingdom and in May 1998 in the US.","title":"Dreamcatcher (Ian Gillan album)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" All songs were performed by Ian Gillan accompanied by Steve Morris.","title":"Dreamcatcher (Ian Gillan album)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The album was being worked on between 1995 and 1997.","title":"Dreamcatcher (Ian Gillan album)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Joe Mennonna is an accomplished session musician who worked with Ian Gillan and Roger Glover on their 1988 album "Accidentally on Purpose", and toured with Ian Gillan in September 2006 in support of the "Gillan's Inn" album.","title":"Joe Mennonna"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He also appears on Gillan's "Live in Anaheim".","title":"Joe Mennonna"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Raymond John Fenwick (born 18 July 1946) is an English guitarist and session musician, best known for replacing Steve Howe in The Syndicats, and as the lead guitarist of Ian Gillan's post Deep Purple solo project, the Ian Gillan Band.","title":"Ray Fenwick"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: musician
